{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3","id":855543,"title":"Will Abyssals still be \"dark reflections\" in Ex3?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T00:41:41-07:00","id":855543,"title":"Will Abyssals still be \"dark reflections\" in Ex3?","content":"In 2nd edition, Abyssal exaltations were corrupted Solar exaltations.<br /> <br /> The Ex3 backer PDF also makes some insinuations to that effect, with Abyssals having very comparable powers and charms to the Solars (Attribute + Ability Excellency, third circle of sorcery/necromancy, Elegant Flowing Deflection meet Dipping Swallow Defense, etc).<br /> <br /> But the last I heard, exaltations would no longer be roaming bullets of magical awesome in Ex3. What would that make Abyssal exaltation? Is Sol also empowering the Deathknights? If so why? If not, then where are their powers coming from and why do they so closely resemble Solar powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-30-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:03:49-07:00","id":855558,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure they're still the twisted Solars, made by the Deathlords using the stolen power of the Sun. Jade Prison is still a thing, so I presume the part where the DLs crack it open and grab the accumulated Solar Essence will still hold true as well. The details of the process may differ, or they may remain undisclosed this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T02:12:42-07:00","id":855589,"title":"","content":"Even Second Edition didn't have Abyssal Essences as something that roamed freely, unless their controlling Monstrance was destroyed. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, then where are their powers coming from and why do they so closely resemble Solar powers?</div> </div> </div> </div> By the will of the Unconquered Sun, the Solar Exalted are returning from death. The Deathlords, terribly mighty and drawing secrets from the tombs of the Neverborn, have done something awesome and blasphemous to appropriate some of those returning Essences, making Solars who truly are returning from the grave, proof of the thesis that Solars inevitably darken and doom the world, Lawgivers for worlds beyond the veil or at the end of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T09:38:22-07:00","id":855746,"title":"","content":"Headcanon aside, we don't know whether the nature of Abyssal Exaltations will be the same this time around as it was. I don't expect the writers to discard the basic conceit that they represent the power of a Solar Exaltation, stolen and twisted by the power of the Underworld. The existence of Black Market Exaltations actually suggests a setting where such a thing is entirely plausible. But the metaphysics of how and why this happened may well be different. We haven't been told enough to say anything more certain at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:02:24-07:00","id":855760,"title":"","content":"&quot;Dark reflection&quot; always came across as kind of a meaningless &quot;edgy&quot; buzzword, implemented with boring mechanics, so at that rate, I sure hope not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:22:10-07:00","id":855769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3#post855543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the last I heard, exaltations would no longer be roaming bullets of magical awesome in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as &quot;they will be directed bullets of magical awesome&quot;. So, they will still be corruptible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:23:08-07:00","id":855770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855760#post855760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dark reflection&quot; always came across as kind of a meaningless &quot;edgy&quot; buzzword, implemented with boring mechanics, so at that rate, I sure hope not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of Abyssals as Solars' dark reflection is sound, it's the execution that was flawed for two editions in a row.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:28:21-07:00","id":855777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855770#post855770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of Abyssals as Solars' dark reflection is sound, it's the execution that was flawed for two editions in a row.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but those two things are so inextricably intertwined, that the failures of the latter do reflect on the soundness/interestingness of the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:40:57-07:00","id":855781,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what's wrong with Abyssals being dark reflections.<br /> <br /> Solars are associated with the light and Creation. Abyssals are associated with darkness and the Underworld. If we're going to call that edgy, then Persephone and Ra are edgy. Both of them are associated with life and both descend into the underworld and are transformed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:44:59-07:00","id":855786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855781#post855781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea what's wrong with Abyssals being dark reflections.<br /> <br /> Solars are associated with the light and Creation. Abyssals are associated with darkness and the Underworld. If we're going to call that edgy, then Persephone and Ra are edgy. Both of them are associated with life and both descend into the underworld and are transformed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Abyssals just need some better charms (and limit break mechanics)... you know like every other non-Solar/Infernal splat that was in Ex2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-30-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:49:58-07:00","id":855788,"title":"","content":"And there is something to be said about possibility of redemption back into Solar. I'd rather play a good abyssal who's content with his state, but I can see redemption being a cool possibility.<br /> <br /> And vice versa.<br /> <br /> &quot;Being Abyssal is WRONG&quot; can go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","user":"Runelord","date":". 03-30-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:53:57-07:00","id":855793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855777#post855777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but those two things are so inextricably intertwined, that the failures of the latter do reflect on the soundness/interestingness of the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably, they botched it at such an early design stage that it doesn't really reflect on the idea. To paraphrase John from the KS backer teaser, previous editions got the part that makes Abyssals feel like Solars, but never figured out the part that makes them different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:59:25-07:00","id":855797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runelord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855788#post855788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there is something to be said about possibility of redemption back into Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>mehhhhhhhhhhh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:02:43-07:00","id":855802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855797#post855797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mehhhhhhhhhhh</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to completely kill that plot option, but it would be nice if it wasn't the default &quot;My Abyssal isn't a complete evil bastard, so I need to become Solar to prove that.&quot; <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:06:32-07:00","id":855805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855781#post855781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are associated with the light and Creation. Abyssals are associated with darkness and the Underworld. If we're going to call that edgy, then Persephone and Ra are edgy. Both of them are associated with life and both descend into the underworld and are transformed</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals and Solars never really interacted with the mythic dichotomy you're describing. I say &quot;dark reflection&quot; as an Abyssal theme was &quot;edgy&quot; (quotes included, because it was a failed concept) because all it did was played up stereotypes for both gothic aesthetics (without much associated goth culture) and general eeeeeevil that seemed to be reminiscent of the Sabbat, but just never got equivalent depth of concept or meaningful goal structure that players could actually buy in to without being idiots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855802#post855802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to completely kill that plot option, but it would be nice if it wasn't the default &quot;My Abyssal isn't a complete evil bastard, so I need to become Solar to prove that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't mind killing that plot option. You made a choice, reap what you sow. Redemption to me flies in the face of actions having permanent consequences. Also yeah it was 1000000% overdone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:11:32-07:00","id":855812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855805#post855805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I don't mind killing that plot option. You made a choice, reap what you sow. Redemption to me flies in the face of actions having permanent consequences. Also yeah it was 1000000% overdone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buyer's Remorse should be a character option for Abyssals. <br /> <br /> Though in my opinion, Redemption should require the death of the current Abyssal (you cheated death, now you need embrace it). The Exaltation's next incarnation can be a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:13:22-07:00","id":855815,"title":"","content":"I'm all for NPCs claiming that being Abyssal is wrong. Food for kill-sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:15:59-07:00","id":855818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855812#post855812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buyer's Remorse should be a character option for Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buyer's remorse doesn't mean you're entitled to have an out. Caveat emptor. :P <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855812#post855812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though in my opinion, Redemption should require the death of the current Abyssal (you cheated death, now you need embrace it). The Exaltation's next incarnation can be a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably fine. The big issue for me is that, in my experience, basically every PC Abyssal's story turns into a redemption story, unless you're playing loyalists, which...I've done a couple times and still am not sure how it is supposed to work without you on the OOC level just going <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><i>\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af </i></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:22:04-07:00","id":855825,"title":"","content":"In my experience, STs and other players straight up tell you they'll force you into redemption or kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:23:21-07:00","id":855826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855818#post855818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The big issue for me is that, in my experience, basically every PC Abyssal's story turns into a redemption story</div> </div> </div> </div>The advantage of being relatively new* to Exalted is that I have only played one game with an Abyssal and that character's arc had nothing to do with Redemption.<br /> <br /> *was introduced when Dreams of the First Age came out and took a ~five year sojourn into Fate/Indie Games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T11:56:59-07:00","id":855854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855826#post855826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The advantage of being relatively new* to Exalted is that I have only played one game with an Abyssal and that character's arc had nothing to do with Redemption.<br /> <br /> *was introduced when Dreams of the First Age came out and took a ~five year sojourn into Fate/Indie Games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the end I was starting to consider <b>maybe</b> pursuing redemption, but I think that was more he was starting to think maybe he's not guaranteed dead, and it was far more likely he tries to pick up an apprentice or something other than &quot;I'm a monster if I'm not a solar&quot;. Did everyone forget Solars have an infinitely longer rap sheet than abyssals? I mean seriously Wonder's solar had caused far more destruction than my abyssal ever did in that campaign. I'm just hoping the mirror mechanic is dead and buried, preferably with a return to the making everyone else worse mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:04:01-07:00","id":855863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855854#post855854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean seriously Wonder's solar had caused far more destruction than my abyssal ever did in that campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, now. If it wasn't for your Abyssal's resonance bomb, my Solar wouldn't had to roll Limit. Five Successes* later, my Twilight is walking into Lookshy with 8 points of Limit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *I rolled two tens and an eight on three dice. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:08:21-07:00","id":855865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855818#post855818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably fine. The big issue for me is that, in my experience, basically every PC Abyssal's story turns into a redemption story, unless you're playing loyalists, which...I've done a couple times and still am not sure how it is supposed to work without you on the OOC level just going <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system-font\"><i>\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af </i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the risk of that happening again will need to be reassessed once we know more about 3e Abyssals, from their degree of mechanical playability to the breadth and depth of their narrative potential from the players' perspective to how much the writing impresses upon readers that the Abyssal condition is undesireable.<br /> <br /> It's not that surprising that the redemption story dominated the Abyssal play experience in 2e, since both the mechanics and the story of Abyssals presented them as something you don't want to be in the long run, plus there is some appeal in the perspective of a successful redemption arc making your character a little extra special (both narratively and mechanically). I hope the incentives will be distributed differently for 3e Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:16:03-07:00","id":855876,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think a big change that could be made is emphasizing how the Abyssal condition may be <i>unnatural </i>but not presenting it as<i> totally undesirable</i> in the long run (let alone &quot;world-killing&quot;), or whatnot. This will undoubtedly also tie in with presentation of the Deathlords and Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:22:04-07:00","id":855882,"title":"","content":"It was resonance bomb or try to politically maneuver against the Silver Prince, considering all of our character's were socially inept it was a good idea at the time :c<br /> I still argue Solars are debatably more dangerous than abyssals because Solars aren't immediately seen as bad guys to the entirety of creation (only most of it).<br /> You rolled limit twice in Lookshy so RNG balanced out in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:32:05-07:00","id":855946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ferryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855746#post855746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of Black Market Exaltations actually suggests a setting where such a thing is entirely plausible. But the metaphysics of how and why this happened may well be different. We haven't been told enough to say anything more certain at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh now there's an important point I completely forgot about. Does anyone have a page number for the backer PDF so I can look up what is said canonically about trading in exaltations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855812#post855812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buyer's Remorse should be a character option for Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree with this, as part and parcel of a good gothic horror story is a feeling of &quot;otherness&quot; and discomfort in your own condition. But as Zelbinnean said, &quot;unnatural&quot; gives you the same story options as &quot;undesirable&quot; and doesn't limit your mechanics as much. Having 99.99% of living beings think that you are a world-slaying abomination is more than enough impetus to fuel a redemption arch I think. Resonance and institutional enslavement were always a ham-fisted narrative device to enforce an unpleasant game experience without adding any real content to the splat.<br /> <br /> And for the record, I was pretty disappointed to see Elegant Flowing Defense in the sample Abyssal package. I would have been more than happy to see this plot element buried, but I still don't see how it can even function in a setting where Sol has personal control over where his exaltations go. Even if that control is somewhat subliminal, I just can't imagine him investing his power in CoDs without a pretty compelling narrative device.<br /> <br /> [EDIT] As a thought, maybe the Deathlords scrounged up enough First Age solar ghosts to use in the creation of a pseudo-exaltation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:48:52-07:00","id":855964,"title":"","content":"Pertinent quotes from the What We Know wiki:<br /> <br /> <i>Q: Will Abyssals still be altered Solar Exaltations? <b>(Mockery)</b></i><br /> A: Yes. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> <br /> <i>(on why Abyssals remain altered Solars)</i><br /> Throwing out the castes might as well be throwing out the book. &quot;Dark Solars&quot; continues to be a concept that fires my imagination, far more than &quot;Exalt of the [Oblivion/Void/other generic concept]&quot; ever will, and that the game has pushed them in that direction in 2e is one of the number one reasons why they went from arguably the most popular splat in 1e to the hands-down least popular splat in 2e. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> <br /> No Mirror Keyword. You can't have a Charm set that is an expression of Ability skill and apexes in a display of peak skill or power and also have that Charm set contain a body of Charms that a Solar cannot have. The idea is not to challenge the paradigm of &quot;Abyssals are Solars&quot; but to embrace it, and then concentrate on what else they are so that they feel different. Being a Solar transformed into this thing means feeling like a Solar but also feeling like something else. Being subtle and substantial is the trick, and it took looking at what the design of the Solar Charm set is really pointing at to see how to point the Abyssal Charm set at something else. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> <br /> It is stylistically accurate to depict the Abyssals as having deep connections to the Solars. EX3 Abyssals are radically different than they have been in previous editions. Having some identical Charms to Solars is a benefit, rather than a subtraction, because it emphasizes the fact that they were / are Solars, while also making them something else. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:04:34-07:00","id":856033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3#post855543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ex3 backer PDF also makes some insinuations to that effect, with Abyssals having very comparable powers and charms to the Solars (Attribute + Ability Excellency, third circle of sorcery/necromancy, Elegant Flowing Deflection meet Dipping Swallow Defense, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of Solar Mirrors in the Abyssal statblocks was just me taking the path of least resistance to make sure they were at the right power level. They shouldn't be considered indicative of anything the actual Abyssals will look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:47:59-07:00","id":856045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855760#post855760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dark reflection&quot; always came across as kind of a meaningless &quot;edgy&quot; buzzword, implemented with boring mechanics, so at that rate, I sure hope not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a dark reflection has the potential to be an awesome idea, but at the same time an evil black-suited version of the hero is probably lowest hanging branch out there when building an antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:11:17-07:00","id":856059,"title":"","content":"I feel I could do with reading more dying Earth fiction myself, such as the actual Dying Earth series and the Book of the New Sun and the like, but what I can glean from it... when you've got Abyssals who are an effective combination of that kind of pulp hero wandering through a world on the brink of its end (which is also fairly evident in Vampire Hunter D, which is another thing people have often wanted as an Abyssal inspiration), and then <i>combine</i> those with some of the heroes of the gothic and macabre and Byronic, with their melancholy introspection and gloomy moods and aesthetics, I think you've both got a firm base for establishing the thesis of the Abyssal Exalted as internally coherent without relying on basic villainy <i>and</i> making them feel like an organic contrast with the Solar Exalted culture hero, including a basis for desiring a transition between one and the other that doesn't need to be about straightforward moral dichotomies.<br /> <br /> I like the part where prospective Abyssals have to be offered and accept their particular mantle, almost purely for how it all feels very fitting as a mythic narrative, but have lost a lot of tolerance for it being used as a big judgemental cudgel to whack them over the head with (which, possibly unfairly, I currently attribute a lot to Nephilpal's hang ups showing through his work; see also akuma, his whole elaborate thesis on how throwing away your heroic agency means you're a contemptible loser who deserves to have your personality scooped out).<br /> <br /> I think using straightforward surface terms such as &quot;Redemption&quot; serves about the same purpose as calling the Exalted in general &quot;heroes&quot;; that using the traditional terminology in the text while leaving the questions and implications in subtext provokes more introspection, with too much analysis and clarification to relieve postmodern anxieties being something that might make it kind of intolerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:29:29-07:00","id":856067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856045#post856045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a dark reflection has the potential to be an awesome idea, but at the same time an evil black-suited version of the hero is probably lowest hanging branch out there when building an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get out of my brain and stop saying the things in it better than me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:56:08-07:00","id":856113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855964#post855964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pertinent quotes from the What We Know wiki:</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for posting I hadn't read these.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855964#post855964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Q: Will Abyssals still be altered Solar Exaltations? <b>(Mockery)</b></i><br /> A: Yes. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b><br /> <br /> Throwing out the castes might as well be throwing out the book. &quot;Dark Solars&quot; continues to be a concept that fires my imagination, far more than &quot;Exalt of the [Oblivion/Void/other generic concept]&quot; ever will, and that the game has pushed them in that direction in 2e is one of the number one reasons why they went from arguably the most popular splat in 1e to the hands-down least popular splat in 2e. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but can we get a show of hands on how many people agree with John here? Because death themes are very much the things that keep <i>me</i> coming back to play Abyssals year after year, <i>not</i> their Solar-ness. Personally, I think it was limited narrative freedom outside of an &quot;evil solar&quot; concept that ruined Abyssals in 2e, not death themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855964#post855964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Mirror Keyword. You can't have a Charm set that is an expression of Ability skill and apexes in a display of peak skill or power and also have that Charm set contain a body of Charms that a Solar cannot have. The idea is not to challenge the paradigm of &quot;Abyssals are Solars&quot; but to embrace it, and then concentrate on what else they are so that they feel different. Being a Solar transformed into this thing means feeling like a Solar but also feeling like something else. Being subtle and substantial is the trick, and it took looking at what the design of the Solar Charm set is really pointing at to see how to point the Abyssal Charm set at something else. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Am I reading this wrong? Because to me the breakdown reads like &quot;There will be no Mirror keyword charms in Ex3. This is because we don't want Abyssals doing things that Solars can do <i>and </i> things they cannot do. Therefore we will make them even more like Solars in Ex3, and limit their ability to do other things.&quot;<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> hope I'm misinterpreting him here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=855964#post855964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is stylistically accurate to depict the Abyssals as having deep connections to the Solars. EX3 Abyssals are radically different than they have been in previous editions. Having some identical Charms to Solars is a benefit, rather than a subtraction, because it emphasizes the fact that they were / are Solars, while also making them something else. <b>(John M\u00f8rke)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Having an exalt splat to serve as &quot;anti-hero&quot; to the Solar's &quot;hero&quot; (with quotes) is certainly fertile design space, I get that. Still concerned that this points to a ramping up of that concept at the expense of new, unique charm themes though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:09:18-07:00","id":856119,"title":"","content":"I found that quote about exaltation black markets!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ex3 Backer's PDF</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Corruptible. Before being catalyzed into Exaltation, the divine power of the Unconquered Sun may be stolen or traded, perhaps even falling into the hands of criminal or forbidden gods. Some Exigents are the result of such illicit Exaltations, while others are worse\u2014Exaltations altered or polluted as they passed through the divine black market, producing monstrous Exalts of terrible, blasphemous power and nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is in reference to Exigents, specifically. Gods can make their own Chosen, but they require the consent and power of the UCS to do so. My take here is that the power of the UCS can be stolen in transit. Maybe it takes a physical form that the God uses to make an exigent, and in some cases gods sell this unused essence or have it stolen from them before an exigent is made? If we try to fit the Jade Prison into this, maybe this is the place Sol's power was locked away while the Solars were gone, though that would not explain how he kept making exigents.<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel like this raises more questions than it answers. Which might not be a bad thing for a core book.<br /> <br /> [EDIT]Increasingly, my head canon is becoming that the &quot;Jade Prison&quot; is actually a reference to the Jade Pleasure Palace that Sol has been unable to turn away from since retiring from Creation's affairs in disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-30-2016, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:22:55-07:00","id":856129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856113#post856113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <i>really</i> hope I'm misinterpreting him here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are. Note he said they'll have &quot;some&quot; of the same charms.<br /> <br /> Look at the Abyssal charms in the antagonist section. The really basic stuff, like Onslaught negators, and pretty much the same. But then there's much more Abyssal stuff above it on the tree, like commanding zombies, crippling people (love that charm), etc.<br /> <br /> I think that the basic bread-and-butter stuff is going to be the same, or almost the same (because, hey, why not: a basic ability charm for stabbing more effectively is going to look pretty similar) while all the thematic stuff will be different.<br /> This likely means that an Essence 1 Solar and Abyssal will be a bit similar, while an Essence 5 Solar and Abyssal will be very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-30-2016, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:24:19-07:00","id":856132,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the whole &quot;Solar Charms point at the Unconquered Sun, while Abyssal Charms start as inversions of that and then point at the Deathlords&quot; thing didn't stop being a thing just because people hated the specific implementation of it that was previewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 03-30-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:58:35-07:00","id":856153,"title":"","content":"My hope is that changing back into a Solar remains a thing that can hypothetically happen, but there's no explanation of how to achieve it and canonically no one ever has. This way it can be something that's always on the horizon if you're into that, but the narrative focus is on the journey rather than the destination, and it's reasonable for other Abyssals to say 'I don't think it's possible, I'm just going to make the best of my lot&quot;. More like Golconda, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T19:30:05-07:00","id":856176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856129#post856129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This likely means that an Essence 1 Solar and Abyssal will be a bit similar, while an Essence 5 Solar and Abyssal will be very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could get behind that. Like you said, a basic damage adder isn't going to look that different from the outside, and it doesn't need to be tremendously different mechanically. The Essence 3+ range of charms would be a nice place to start branching off into different concepts and themes for both splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:19:14-07:00","id":856201,"title":"","content":"I mean, I'm not arguing that all Essence 1 charms should be exactly the same (I hope they're not, because it's not that interesting), but yeah, I think that a lot of basic stuff is going to be similar, especially the dice-based stuff. (No point changing a charm that gives you double 9s on a roll.) With more overtly magical things being much more different (and so, since higher Essence charms tend to be less just basic ability-extensions and more overtly magical, that's why I'd expect Abyssals to be less and less similar as they rise in Essence).<br /> Some charmsets may be more different to others for thematic reasons.<br /> I mean, Solar melee makes you really good at stabbing people. Abyssal melee presumably makes you really good at stabbing people too, just maybe in a more savage and brutal way (and without any of the Holy Warrior stuff).<br /> Whereas Abyssal medicine is probably full of stuff like eating people for health, enhancing zombies, spreading disease, etc. So it's probably a lot more different.<br /> I noticed that Abyssal War seems to have a lot of stuff about necromancy, raising zombies and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:44:27-07:00","id":856248,"title":"","content":"Personally I liked &quot;Chosen of the Void.&quot; more than the whole death schtick. I have other games where I can play a necro guy, but few where I can mess around with the powers of oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T00:19:44-07:00","id":856322,"title":"","content":"What powers were those?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:03:57-07:00","id":856363,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can't really see what the powers of the void were, in a way that was different to the powers of death.<br /> <br /> Void: destroy everything<br /> <br /> Death: destroy everything that's alive, while manipulating/championing ghosts, zombies, etc.<br /> <br /> That seems much more interesting to me.<br /> <br /> Also, while there is some mileage to the &quot;I can do this in other games, I don't need to do it in Exalted&quot; idea... Exalted still has a wider range of things that it can handle, so I see no need to strip it of things just because they're in other games. I mean, I'm not suggesting there be dwarves and elves and orcs all over the place, but while I can play a Necromancer in DnD, I can't really play a death-themed social crafting bureaucrat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:32:52-07:00","id":856370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856363#post856363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I can't really see what the powers of the void were, in a way that was different to the powers of death.<br /> <br /> Void: destroy everything<br /> <br /> Death: destroy everything that's alive, while manipulating/championing ghosts, zombies, etc.<br /> <br /> That seems much more interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started a thread to discuss this very thing, and it's not destroy everything. Not even remotely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T03:36:43-07:00","id":856371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856113#post856113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but can we get a show of hands on how many people agree with John here? Because death themes are very much the things that keep <i>me</i> coming back to play Abyssals year after year, <i>not</i> their Solar-ness. Personally, I think it was limited narrative freedom outside of an &quot;evil solar&quot; concept that ruined Abyssals in 2e, not death themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals' connection to Solars was always indispensable to my understanding of them. It gives them a place in the setting's overarching narrative that no generic chosen of death could fill - the Lawgivers of old, come back from the dead to take revenge on the world that betrayed and murdered them. Abyssals as something that just crawled out of the Mouth of the Void would never have this much gravitas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:07:09-07:00","id":856390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856370#post856370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I started a thread to discuss this very thing, and it's not destroy everything. Not even remotely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll be honest, I didn't find oblivion-as-forgetting that interesting either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:13:44-07:00","id":856395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started a thread to discuss this very thing, and it's not destroy everything. Not even remotely.</div> </div> </div> </div> What, does &quot;void&quot; mean forgotten and disregarded as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:16:23-07:00","id":856398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856390#post856390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'll be honest, I didn't find oblivion-as-forgetting that interesting either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the thing, everyone has their own tastes. Frankly, I think &quot;dark solars&quot; is... it's so WoD vampires, which makes sense. But it doesn't feel Exalted. It feels like Solars in black trenchcoats with katanas and sunglasses on at all times. At least if it's the ONLY theme to them. But we'll see how it is in 3rd ed. Maybe I'll be happily surprised.<br /> <br /> And focusing on death is something we've seen and it... really wasn't that much better than the vampires.<br /> <br /> I want Abyssals that have even some of the potential they have fulfilled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856395#post856395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What, does &quot;void&quot; mean forgotten and disregarded as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oblivion means that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:11:55-07:00","id":856420,"title":"","content":"Abyssals draw obvious inspiration from vampires, from their gothic imagery that's at odds with the swords-and-sandals feel of the rest of the setting, to their state of walking the boundary between life and death, to the fact that they can (or at least could) drink blood to replenish their strength.<br /> <br /> None of this is predicated on their link with Solars, though, as Solars have nothing in common with vampires. I'd argue their vampiric themes are the only thing that clearly distinguishes them from Solars in editions past.<br /> <br /> That, and I'll take death over Oblivion as their thematic basis any day. Death is the intrinsic part of the human experience, which both grounds the Abyssals and lets them draw from the wealth of inspirations, stories and folklore across all times, places and cultures. Oblivion, on the other hand, is a very particular, narrow and artificial view of death that may have worked for Wraith (which I've never played, so I don't know), but doesn't really work with the cosmology and themes of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:12:11-07:00","id":856421,"title":"","content":"I mean, the role of each ability in combat can change too. We've already seen a very strong flavor for Melee, Thrown, Brawl and Archery for Solars. Brawl isn't just unarmed punchkilling, it's single-target onslaught-stacking soak penetrating hardness-ignoring clash-loving nonsense. Thrown has a million disarms, ways to strike immediately, and strike from stealth. Archery lets you shoot your intimacies into people. Etc, etc. If Abyssal Brawl follows the same core path of just being the onslaught-based single target destruction, I'd be severely disappointed; there's room to make Abyssal Thrown incredibly different from Solar Thrown just by making it not be the Abyssal Alpha-Strike-From-Stealth ability, before you even get into slathering everything with a big bucket of black paint and supergluing skeletons to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:58:45-07:00","id":856443,"title":"","content":"Exalted's underworld and Oblivion are very different (and frankly, the underworld is bland and practically pointless feeling) from Wraith. Exalted took some things without understanding why they worked in Wraith, and removing a lot of things that could have worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:43:31-07:00","id":856466,"title":"","content":"The big problem I have with Oblivion in Exalted is that its role as horrible existential threat and an unnatural end of things falls flat on me, because it's not that different functionally from the alleged &quot;good end&quot; that is Lethe. If both mean the absolute and utter annihilation of everything that defined you as a person, what's so scary about Oblivion again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:51:39-07:00","id":856471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856466#post856466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem I have with Oblivion in Exalted is that its role as horrible existential threat and an unnatural end of things falls flat on me, because it's not that different functionally from the alleged &quot;good end&quot; that is Lethe. If both mean the absolute and utter annihilation of everything that defined you as a person, what's so scary about Oblivion again?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To the individual, it is the same result, but on an aggregate level, there is a major difference. In Ex2 &quot;define everything&quot; setting, I assume destruction of the soul is detrimental to the stability of Creation. If enough souls embrace Oblivion could have dire consequences, blah blah blah. <br /> <br /> Sort of like the difference between recycling a can or throwing it out. To an individual's day to day life, there is no difference between the two except which bin you throw it in. Someone comes and takes the can away. But on an aggregate level, all those cans in the landfill do have an impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:54:06-07:00","id":856473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856466#post856466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem I have with Oblivion in Exalted is that its role as horrible existential threat and an unnatural end of things falls flat on me, because it's not that different functionally from the alleged &quot;good end&quot; that is Lethe. If both mean the absolute and utter annihilation of everything that defined you as a person, what's so scary about Oblivion again?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact is, that's a part of my problems (a big part even) Morangias. Oblivion became sorta like Lethe's evil, mustache twirling twin. Which is not just boring, but causes issues with most Underworld stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:47:52-07:00","id":856505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856471#post856471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the individual, it is the same result, but on an aggregate level, there is a major difference. In Ex2 &quot;define everything&quot; setting, I assume destruction of the soul is detrimental to the stability of Creation. If enough souls embrace Oblivion could have dire consequences, blah blah blah.<br /> <br /> Sort of like the difference between recycling a can or throwing it out. To an individual's day to day life, there is no difference between the two except which bin you throw it in. Someone comes and takes the can away. But on an aggregate level, all those cans in the landfill do have an impact.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you noted yourself, the difference only makes sense if you embrace 2e's spirit of explaining everything in unnecessary detail and making you care about the grand cosmological ramifications of things, which is not something most people want to be concerned with, even in a rather cerebral game like Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856473#post856473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact is, that's a part of my problems (a big part even) Morangias. Oblivion became sorta like Lethe's evil, mustache twirling twin. Which is not just boring, but causes issues with most Underworld stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't play Wraith, but I did skim the 1e corebook which was available for free on DrivethruRPG at some point. From what I remember, nobody in Wraith knew what happens to those who pass on. This makes a world of difference, compared to Exalted, because in Wraith, your options as a ghost were to continue in the crapsack Underworld, cease existing or brave the Great Unknown, which was appropriately bleak, but still left a sliver of hope for something better. In Exalted, however, the options are to continue in the crapsack Underworld, cease existing, or cease existing in a different way that may be bad for the world at large. When a game of epic heroes at the dawn of time manages to be more bleak than the bleakest segment of a larger setting called World of Darkness, something went wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:59:30-07:00","id":856512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856505#post856505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you noted yourself, the difference only makes sense if you embrace 2e's spirit of explaining everything in unnecessary detail and making you care about the grand cosmological ramifications of things, which is not something most people want to be concerned with, even in a rather cerebral game like Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that isn't the way Exalted should portray Oblivion. It was just a metaphor I use to explain the difference between Lethe and Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Hell, it's difficult enough to get people to recycle, much less not consign your soul to Oblivion for ultimate powers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:04:33-07:00","id":856515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856505#post856505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you noted yourself, the difference only makes sense if you embrace 2e's spirit of explaining everything in unnecessary detail and making you care about the grand cosmological ramifications of things, which is not something most people want to be concerned with, even in a rather cerebral game like Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't play Wraith, but I did skim the 1e corebook which was available for free on DrivethruRPG at some point. From what I remember, nobody in Wraith knew what happens to those who pass on. This makes a world of difference, compared to Exalted, because in Wraith, your options as a ghost were to continue in the crapsack Underworld, cease existing or brave the Great Unknown, which was appropriately bleak, but still left a sliver of hope for something better. In Exalted, however, the options are to continue in the crapsack Underworld, cease existing, or cease existing in a different way that may be bad for the world at large. When a game of epic heroes at the dawn of time manages to be more bleak than the bleakest segment of a larger setting called World of Darkness, something went wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like your problem isn't with Oblivion at all, but rather with reincarnation.<br /> <br /> I mean, many people in the world believe in reincarnation, and would definitely, absolutely, rather be reincarnated than cease to exist, even though they know that people (well, except maybe some lamas) lose all their memories.<br /> Not saying they're right, just that it's how most people (but perhaps not all! Hence ghosts) in the setting will feel about it.<br /> <br /> Which... I guess is not a very good reason for you to care.<br /> I'm fine with it, personally.<br /> <br /> I mean, essentially, I'd much rather get retrograde amnesia and forget who I am entirely, than die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:33:57-07:00","id":856579,"title":"","content":"It's not the reincarnation in general that I have a problem with, it's the particular flavor of reincarnation presented in Exalted, which makes it pretty much pointless, just a perfectly utilitarian mechanism for handling the souls of the lesser beings designed by mad titans who couldn't give a fuck about human life even if they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:37:17-07:00","id":856581,"title":"","content":"Hey, Oz, feel like continuing that discussion we had the <i>last</i> time the subject of reincarnation and identity came up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:59:43-07:00","id":856601,"title":"","content":"Are there actually any concepts of reincarnation that don't assume a fair bit is lost or repressed in the transition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:16:53-07:00","id":856644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856371#post856371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals' connection to Solars was always indispensable to my understanding of them. It gives them a place in the setting's overarching narrative that no generic chosen of death could fill - the Lawgivers of old, come back from the dead to take revenge on the world that betrayed and murdered them. Abyssals as something that just crawled out of the Mouth of the Void would never have this much gravitas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well okay then. Give the people what they want, I'm apparently more of a hedge case than I thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals draw obvious inspiration from vampires, from their gothic imagery that's at odds with the swords-and-sandals feel of the rest of the setting, to their state of walking the boundary between life and death, to the fact that they can (or at least could) drink blood to replenish their strength. None of this is predicated on their link with Solars, though, as Solars have nothing in common with vampires. I'd argue their vampiric themes are the only thing that clearly distinguishes them from Solars in editions past.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were to boil the themes of this down, I'd say the core difference here is adding a theme of consumption to a superman archetype. In many stories, especially the pulp fiction that heavily influences Exalted, Vampires are supermen equivalent to any other big bad in the setting, with the only drawback being that they have to kill or at least harm the living to survive. If Solars are pulp hero supermen archetypes, then would you take a deal to get those same powers knowing that you'd have to keep killing people to maintain them? What do you care about enough to make that worth it?<br /> <br /> It's a great foil and theme for Abyssals to have and maintain, but it does come with some challenges. For one thing, the player can just as easily choose to play a normal superman without this serious handicap. Why would you choose to play the inferior product, many would ask (I am infamous for loading up on flaws and disadvantages, so this is not a question that troubles me). For another, the core theme of the Solar charmset is &quot;excellence&quot; so taking that power also means copy-pasting a lot of those charms over in a frankly quite boring way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and I'll take death over Oblivion as their thematic basis any day. Death is the intrinsic part of the human experience, which both grounds the Abyssals and lets them draw from the wealth of inspirations, stories and folklore across all times, places and cultures. Oblivion, on the other hand, is a very particular, narrow and artificial view of death that may have worked for Wraith (which I've never played, so I don't know), but doesn't really work with the cosmology and themes of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death and the Underworld are pretty indispensable to Deathknights, but Oblivion is also important. As has been pointed out, reincarnation via Lethe can be interpreted several ways depending on philosophy. The degree to which you will see Lethe and Oblivion as indistinguishable comes down to whether or not you think a person <i>is</i> their memories. If Lethe canonically becomes the complete destruction of ego and perspective, then Oblivion becomes unnecessary. But what is important is that there be some canonical fashion in which things in Exalted cease to be and never come back from, to maintain the possibility of true loss. Because loss is the cornerstone of tragedy, and Abyssals are tragic antiheroes. Not &quot;tragic&quot; in the sense of &quot;cannot accomplish anything and ruins everything they touch&quot; as they were in Ex2, but tragic in the sense that they know they can't save everyone, and that what's been lost can't always be returned.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think a division of death and Oblivion proper is good for the setting. You have &quot;death is a doorway&quot; in Lethe, where the memories of this life are erased but there is something essentially <i>you</i> left over that gets another lease on life, and then there is &quot;true death&quot; which is the objectively terrifying thing where everything you ever were ceases to be. Oblivion works great as a backdrop to a tragic hero of death story, but not to the cheeseball heroic antics of the Solar exalted. Being able to pick and choose your themes is essential to a setting this big.<br /> <br /> Put another way, in some stories you want the little boy to stay dead, but in others you want them to make a star wars force ghost cameo where he smiles before disappearing into a beam of light once the bad guy is beaten up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:12:01-07:00","id":856678,"title":"","content":"Certainly, if you assume that a soul cleansed of it's memories by Lethe is effectively a blank slate, interchangeable with any other soul, it doesn't look significantly different from oblivion. And given that the society we live in places such a high value on intellectuality and reasoned, logical thought, it's an easy asssumption to fall into. <br /> <br /> I think if you want to avoid that, it's worth not just looking at real world beliefs about reincarnation and past lives, but also looking at them as a story element: why we find the idea fascinating, and continue to tell stories about it. And from the point of view of our stories, it's very clear that events in one life are expected to have some effect on the events of subsequent lives, or else we wouldn't bother making the connection and saying that the one person is a reincarnation of the other.<br /> <br /> In many stories, this connection takes the form of karmic law, where say, a king who waged needless war which brought suffering to his people might be in his next life a peasant in a war-torn country, so that the experiences balance out. This kind of system of cosmic justice really doesn't fit the tone of Exalted, but it this scenario it's pretty clear that the peasant doesn't remember being a king, and probably doesn't have the same personality the king did, his soul still retains information about his choices and experiences in his previous lifetimes.<br /> <br /> Lethe in Exalted is inspired by the river of the same name in Greek philosophy, and it exists to explain why, if people reincarnate over and over again, don't they remembember anything about their past lives? But we don't always remember events of our current lives, yet our present knowledge of pshychology suggest that those events still can have a great deal of impact on how we think and act, especially formative experiences we have as children that are often no longer conciously available to us. Part of how Tibetan monks find the reincarnation of the Dalai Lama is by making very young children select objects from among a group and one who chooses the objects that belonged to previous Dalai Lamas is considered a possible candidate. The children aren't expected to remember anything about their previous lives, but it is still assumed that they would be drawn to the familiar objects rather than the unfamiliar ones.<br /> <br /> We also have stories about people who <i>do</i> remember past lives at least partially, and also people who believe that using specific practices or techniques they can gain access to information about their own or other's past lives. Previous editions of Exalted have included a past life merit, which allows Celestial Exalts to remember events from their previous from their previous incarnations, but is also allowed to Dragonblooded and mortals at low ratings to represent retaining memories of their Hun soul, so perhaps Lethe isn't always perfect either.<br /> <br /> And while little has been written about exactly how the process of reincarnation works in Exalted (probably because this is one of those things where giving STs leeway to do what is right for their games is important) it is clear that Gods can interfere with the process, such as Taru-Han with her collection of souls, and Ahlat, who can make tassels for his cloak from the souls of brave warriors. I don't think it's ever indicated whether politcally powerful gods could somehow influence which soul gets put into which infant, but there are certainly stories one could tell using that idea.<br /> <br /> TL,DR: If you don't want reincarnation to seem pointless, don't assume that it removes all meaningfully distinguishing traits of souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:56:21-07:00","id":856803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856644#post856644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to boil the themes of this down, I'd say the core difference here is adding a theme of consumption to a superman archetype. In many stories, especially the pulp fiction that heavily influences Exalted, Vampires are supermen equivalent to any other big bad in the setting, with the only drawback being that they have to kill or at least harm the living to survive. If Solars are pulp hero supermen archetypes, then would you take a deal to get those same powers knowing that you'd have to keep killing people to maintain them? What do you care about enough to make that worth it?<br /> <br /> It's a great foil and theme for Abyssals to have and maintain, but it does come with some challenges. For one thing, the player can just as easily choose to play a normal superman without this serious handicap. Why would you choose to play the inferior product, many would ask (I am infamous for loading up on flaws and disadvantages, so this is not a question that troubles me). For another, the core theme of the Solar charmset is &quot;excellence&quot; so taking that power also means copy-pasting a lot of those charms over in a frankly quite boring way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It probably isn't going to be a handicap, let alone a serious one. It wasn't really in 1e, and in 2e Abyssals were only nerfed due to carelessness. I'm actually surprised to see that you have a strong sense of Abyssals as inferior, handicapped Solars, because as far as I can tell that's never been their presentation or the intention underlying their design. You're not a V:tM vampire who has to go out and eat people to live or anything like that. Moreover, Abyssals will obviously never be so similar to Solars that there's functionally no difference between the two. That's never been the case -- Abyssals always brought a lot of appealing things that were their own to the table in spite of their link to the Solars.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T18:52:59-07:00","id":856838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856803#post856803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually surprised to see that you have a strong sense of Abyssals as inferior, handicapped Solars, because as far as I can tell that's never been their presentation or the intention underlying their design. You're not a V:tM vampire who has to go out and eat people to live or anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resonance. Starting off as enslaved to a psychotic monster. A charmset that kills and does little else. It might not have been their intention to create an inferior solar solaroid, but sure was the end result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:02:22-07:00","id":856839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856838#post856838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance. Starting off as enslaved to a psychotic monster. A charmset that kills and does little else. It might not have been their intention to create an inferior solar solaroid, but sure was the end result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 2e the Abyssal Charmset did a lot besides kill, and Resonance is balanced against the Great Curse for Solars, which some people actually seem to like less. The &quot;being enslaved&quot; angle has varied a lot over the course of the line, and there has always been the option to play a &quot;free&quot; Abyssal not Deathlord-affiliated at all. Most PC-patron Deathlords people actually seemed to run in practice came off more like &quot;Machiavellian terror Santa&quot; (which was totally within the scope of the intended Abyssal playspace). Like Resonance, we also have reason to think it's being toned down somewhat for 3e.<br /> <br /> It kind of sounds to me like you find Abyssals intrinsically unappealing and are interpreting them in the most uncharitable light possible as a result. All I really have to say in response to that is: remember that 1e's Abyssals were as big a hit as 2e's Infernals. Clearly there are a lot of people who see the appeal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-31-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:00:07-07:00","id":856917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856581#post856581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Oz, feel like continuing that discussion we had the <i>last</i> time the subject of reincarnation and identity came up?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you like, but I don't remember what you were saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wandering</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL,DR: If you don't want reincarnation to seem pointless, don't assume that it removes all meaningfully distinguishing traits of souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I think, is the point.<br /> I think Morangias is right in that reincarnation has been generally presented in a way that makes your previous life far more irrelevant than it has to be.<br /> Though not always. Scroll of Heroes had, in its (yes, I know, terrible) merits section, a Past Life merit.<br /> <br /> But I think the most important way is probably to go with the subtle effects that most (but not orthodox Buddhists) reincarnation philosophies expect. Like you said, being drawn to the same things, having a similar personality, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> That could maybe get mentioned before. I think maybe the issue is that Exalted gets distracted by putting all those things onto Celestial reincarnation, which isn't really reincarnation at all.<br /> <br /> (Often, I just have my characters believe Celestial reincarnation is actually reincarnation, so that they can act like things like Oblivian are horrifying, believe going into Lethe is a good thing, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:02:56-07:00","id":856919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856839#post856839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in 2e the Abyssal Charmset did a lot besides kill, and Resonance is balanced against the Great Curse for Solars, which some people actually seem to like less. The &quot;being enslaved&quot; angle has varied a lot over the course of the line, and there has always been the option to play a &quot;free&quot; Abyssal not Deathlord-affiliated at all. Most PC-patron Deathlords people actually seemed to run in practice came off more like &quot;Machiavellian terror Santa&quot; (which was totally within the scope of the intended Abyssal playspace). Like Resonance, we also have reason to think it's being toned down somewhat for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I flat-out disagree with you here. Resonance is not equivalent to Limit Break. Limit Break is a thing you decide on as a player, to express your character's personality and heroic limitations. In most cases, Limit Breaks make <i>sense</i> even if they aren't convenient, and improve the story. Resonance by contrast is a series of <i>static</i> penalties applied to <i>all</i> Abyssals that enforces a play style of &quot;kill a mortal every five minutes.&quot; Even if you do find this loyalist play style enjoyable, the fact that there were hard mechanics <i>punishing</i> you for playign anythign else was objectively unfun.<br /> <br /> Deathlords are another setting element that is only fun if you embrace the loyalist path. They are Essence 10 Solar-Abyssal hybrids with every charm they qualify for and most stats at ten, and no starting Abyssal has even a slim chance against that when they <i>start off</i> in a position of magical and physical enslavement. The Deathlords have every reason to keep them on an extremely short leash. They might put up with the odd act of kindness here or there, but if you actually want to be free? Your character is a solaroid exaltation, a literally priceless resource that they can kill and recover at <i>any</i> time by using touch-keyword charms through your monstrance. Good luck escaping that if you have an ST that rolls dice for them, ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856839#post856839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of sounds to me like you find Abyssals intrinsically unappealing and are interpreting them in the most uncharitable light possible as a result. All I really have to say in response to that is: remember that 1e's Abyssals were as big a hit as 2e's Infernals. Clearly there are a lot of people who see the appeal!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that's being tremendously unfair. I think the implementation of 2e Abyssals was severely flawed and I see many missed oppurtunities. Addressing those mistakes will be important going forward, hence why I started a thread on the topic of how Abyssals and their relationship to Solars might be changing in Ex3. Just because I don't like the same things about Abyssals you do doesn't mean I hate Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":".  editing for rudeness 04-01-2016, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T21:06:08-07:00","id":856923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856839#post856839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even in 2e the Abyssal Charmset did a lot besides kill, and Resonance is balanced against the Great Curse for Solars, which some people actually seem to like less. The &quot;being enslaved&quot; angle has varied a lot over the course of the line, and there has always been the option to play a &quot;free&quot; Abyssal not Deathlord-affiliated at all. Most PC-patron Deathlords people actually seemed to run in practice came off more like &quot;Machiavellian terror Santa&quot; (which was totally within the scope of the intended Abyssal playspace). Like Resonance, we also have reason to think it's being toned down somewhat for 3e.<br /> <br /> It kind of sounds to me like you find Abyssals intrinsically unappealing and are interpreting them in the most uncharitable light possible as a result. All I really have to say in response to that is: remember that 1e's Abyssals were as big a hit as 2e's Infernals. Clearly there are a lot of people who see the appeal!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be honest, while Resonance was supposed to be balanced against the Great Curse, in practice I found that, unless you were part of an all-evil circle of Abyssals who conquer places with their zombie armies, it was far more awkward. To the extent that I never saw an Abyssal played in a mixed-game for very long. They'd generally have Resonance problems every session, while limit breaks are more like once a story if that. <br /> The only time I saw an Abyssal played in a mixed-game for more than a handful of sessions was when they used the Dark Fate rules from Shards of the Exalted Dream instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:41:59-07:00","id":856959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856919#post856919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I flat-out disagree with you here. Resonance is not equivalent to Limit Break. Limit Break is a thing you decide on as a player, to express your character's personality and heroic limitations. In most cases, Limit Breaks make <i>sense</i> even if they aren't convenient, and improve the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're entitled to your opinion, but there are thousands of pages of knife fights attesting to the fact that many disagree, and this is an answer to the question you posed. If you're asking, &quot;why would <i>I</i> play an Abyssal instead of a Solar?&quot; then the answer might well be &quot;you wouldn't&quot;, but a lot of people have or do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856919#post856919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deathlords are another setting element that is only fun if you embrace the loyalist path. They are Essence 10 Solar-Abyssal hybrids with every charm they qualify for and most stats at ten, and no starting Abyssal has even a slim chance against that when they <i>start off</i> in a position of magical and physical enslavement. The Deathlords have every reason to keep them on an extremely short leash. They might put up with the odd act of kindness here or there, but if you actually want to be free? Your character is a solaroid exaltation, a literally priceless resource that they can kill and recover at <i>any</i> time by using touch-keyword charms through your monstrance. Good luck escaping that if you have an ST that rolls dice for them, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just...begin with a party of Abyssals who are autonomous and not overseen at all, you know. That's a thing. It's always been a thing. Moreover, while the treatment of Deathlords has varied throughout the line, the way you describe them here is cobbled together from all the worst and most extreme portrayals, with a dose of fanon. More to the point, you could easily get rid of all of this without even slightly reducing the Abyssals' themes of vamprism or association with corrupted Solars, which makes it doubly perplexing that that seems to be the angle you're coming at it from.<br /> <br /> (In 1e, I believe Deathlords could only rein in a rogue Abyssal by throwing the monstrance into the Well of Oblivion, which freed their exaltation. I might be misremembering, though.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like that's being tremendously unfair. I think the implementation of 2e Abyssals was severely flawed and I see many missed oppurtunities. Addressing those mistakes will be important going forward, hence why I started a thread on the topic of how Abyssals and their relationship to Solars might be changing in Ex3. Just because I don't like the same things about Abyssals you do doesn't mean I hate Abyssals. </div> </div> </div>I'm curious what you <i>do</i> like about Abyssals (as presented, not in an abstract notion of &quot;death Exalted&quot; as they could alternatively be implemented).<br /> <br /> We agree that 2e's implementation of Abyssals was tremendously flawed (though not perhaps to the extent you're suggesting). But none of this seems to have anything to do with their relationship to Solars or &quot;themes of consumption&quot;, even by your own attesting, and it's pretty broadly acknowledged that 1e's Abyssals (which had nearly identical overall themes) were the better implementation of the splat anyway. The relevant question here is: how good could Abyssals be <i>without</i> changing their relationship to Solars or vampire themes? And it seems clear that they could easily be fantastic. They may not be -- obviously it's too soon to tell -- but if they're not, it certainly won't be because they didn't do these things you're insisting are required to make them appealing.<br /> <br /> In essence: you're barking up the wrong tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-01-2016, 01:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:52:07-07:00","id":856964,"title":"","content":"While I don't agree with you about limit vs resonance, I do agree with your last point. The problems with Abyssals weren't really to do with themes of being dark Solars or having some vampire (or zombie, or ghoul) stuff going on. It's not like vampire themes were massively prominent. They were walking around in the day and so forth.<br /> Mechanically, mirror charms (which were derived from the idea of being dark Solars) were awkward because you had to keep checking the Solar book, and also they were dull. But just because Abyssals are (thematically) dark Solars doesn't mean they need mirror charms. Infernals are still, thematically, corrupted Solars, and their charms are not at all Solar-esque.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:55:49-07:00","id":856965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856964#post856964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't agree with you about limit vs resonance, I do agree with your last point. The problems with Abyssals weren't really to do with themes of being dark Solars or having some vampire (or zombie, or ghoul) stuff going on. It's not like vampire themes were massively prominent. They were walking around in the day and so forth.<br /> Mechanically, mirror charms (which were derived from the idea of being dark Solars) were awkward because you had to keep checking the Solar book, and also they were dull. But just because Abyssals are (thematically) dark Solars doesn't mean they need mirror charms. Infernals are still, thematically, corrupted Solars, and their charms are not at all Solar-esque.</div> </div> </div> </div>I perhaps should clarify that I actually do find 2e Resonance much worse than Limit, and even 1e Resonance was somewhat worse. It just wasn't a well thought out mechanic. But given how extreme people's reactions to Limit Break are, it's clear that much of the fanbase feels otherwise, and Limit Break <i>certainly </i>isn't universally perceived as a sensible, heroic, character-building exercise under the control of the player.<br /> <br /> I like the model of Abyssals having Charms very similar to Solar charms at the low level and then diverging. 1e did this elegantly, 2e did it less so; from the preview I have hopes that we'll be back to doing it elegantly in 3e. But I think the real problem with Mirror was more that it was used carelessly as an expedient, and that it heavily constrained tree shape and size in ways where 1e's &quot;pseudo-mirrors&quot; left more freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-01-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:41:44-07:00","id":857005,"title":"","content":"In general I don't think we'll get anything out of debating the worthiness of our respective settings. It sounds like there are some key differences in interpretation, but ultimately the differences are just that: interpretations of the same text. But I do want to address just one point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856959#post856959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can just...begin with a party of Abyssals who are autonomous and not overseen at all, you know. That's a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this a thing in Ex2? Because I have read the Abyssal book quite extensively and I am sure I can find several statements to the effect that all Abyssal exaltations began unlife bound to monstrances, each in the care of a Deathlord. That means that in order to play a free Deathknight you would have had to escape your Deathlord at some point, which is quite frankly a hopeless task for any essence 1-5 solaroid when you <i>actually</i> examine the stat block for any of the Deathlords in canon. In fact, I challenge you to name one single method by which an Essence 5 Abyssal could realistically expect to escape their Deathlord.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856959#post856959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious what you <i>do</i> like about Abyssals (as presented, not in an abstract notion of &quot;death Exalted&quot; as they could alternatively be implemented).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm, but I <i>do</i> like that they are the exalts of death? Which is absolutely how they are presented? That's pretty much 90% of their draw for me?<br /> <br /> I like zombies, and vampires, and ghosts, and life after death and gothic romance and tragic heroes and life as consumption and scary things of both a sincere and cutie-pie variety. I like heroes with bleak outlooks and monsters that kill to live but still find happiness and friendship and dark avengers who do good but don't care if they are celebrated for doing it. I am pretty much entirely here for the gritty death themes.<br /> <br /> I see the merit of having them serve as dark foils to the shiny Solars but ultimately it's just not my thing and if they trim back the existing focus on death and Oblivion to make room for even more Solar mirror charms then for me that's a total loss because I have absolutely zero investment in exploring the Solar hero archetype using <i>other</i> splats.<br /> <br /> Why do <i>you </i>like them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856959#post856959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We agree that 2e's implementation of Abyssals was tremendously flawed (though not perhaps to the extent you're suggesting). But none of this seems to have anything to do with their relationship to Solars or &quot;themes of consumption&quot;, even by your own attesting, and it's pretty broadly acknowledged that 1e's Abyssals (which had nearly identical overall themes) were the better implementation of the splat anyway. The relevant question here is: how good could Abyssals be <i>without</i> changing their relationship to Solars or vampire themes? And it seems clear that they could easily be fantastic. They may not be -- obviously it's too soon to tell -- but if they're not, it certainly won't be because they didn't do these things you're insisting are required to make them appealing.<br /> <br /> In essence: you're barking up the wrong tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really confused by this comment and I can only assume you've misinterpreted me.<br /> <br /> For starters, I <i>like</i> consumption themes? I think hunger and the means we use to sate it are an essential part of the human experience that can be explored in metaphor using things like vampires, ghouls and yes, the Abyssal exalted, to tell <i>great</i> stories. I'd like to see <i>more </i>of that next edition, not less.<br /> <br /> And I at no point intended to advocate that Abyssals should not be corrupted Solars. I made this thread hoping to establish <i>how</i> that might be true in the new setting because of changes in the way Exaltation works (though I see now that this question has been largely forgotten), <i>not</i> as an argument for this element's erasure. Where I disagree is this idea (seemingly espoused by John Morke) that making Abyssals more like Solars will somehow fix all the problems the splat had last edition. While it's true that a Solar/Abyssal comparison did not look kindly upon the Abyssal last time around, I think we gain nothing trying to balance this by filling in the gaps Abyssals had with more Solar powers.<br /> <br /> I would instead like to see a unique thematic approach for the splat, which <i>all</i> the exalt types<i> should</i> have, that competes with Solar might on its own terms. As I've already said, I think having their early charmset closely resemble, but not mirror, Solar charms before branching out into more uniquely Abyssal themed charms at Essence 3+ is a solid solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-01-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T02:28:02-07:00","id":857034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857005#post857005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would instead like to see a unique thematic approach for the splat, which <i>all</i> the exalt types<i> should</i> have, that competes with Solar might on its own terms. As I've already said, I think having their early charmset closely resemble, but not mirror, Solar charms before branching out into more uniquely Abyssal themed charms at Essence 3+ is a solid solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be shocked and extremely disappointed if Abyssals didn't start getting any uniquely Abyssal charms until E3. That's 25 sessions of playing an emo Solar before you're allowed to actually be a deathknight. Having simple root charms that parallel Solar charms is great, but the uniquely Abyssal stuff should also be available right from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T02:37:54-07:00","id":857037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857034#post857034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would be shocked and extremely disappointed if Abyssals didn't start getting any uniquely Abyssal charms until E3. That's 25 sessions of playing an emo Solar before you're allowed to actually be a deathknight. Having simple root charms that parallel Solar charms is great, but the uniquely Abyssal stuff should also be available right from the start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely agree, sorry if that wasn't clear. I think someone mentioned how the Solar combat charms have these built-in themes now, like how Thrown is almost as much about that first round bum-rush as it is long-distance attacks. Having different secondary focuses might be a good design objective for early Abyssal charms.<br /> <br /> One thing I'd really like to see more of for Abyssals are mechanics that make use of your opponent's ones and failures. Whereas Solar heroes tend to rise to the occasion and get stronger as the opposition gets tougher, Abyssals have more talent for capitalizing on their opponent's mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T02:57:27-07:00","id":857042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857005#post857005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I disagree is this idea (seemingly espoused by John Morke) that making Abyssals more like Solars will somehow fix all the problems the splat had last edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, John's idea is to start from the theme of excellence Abyssals share with Solars, and make their flashier stuff express the themes of the Deathlords just as Solars' flashy stuff expresses the themes of UCS. That doesn't sound like making them more like Solars if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:14:56-07:00","id":857067,"title":"","content":"That's how it seems to me too. Which I think is a good idea.<br /> <br /> I expect that, in practice, they'll be less like Solars mechanically, in terms of their charms. Certainly the previewed charms were more different, as are (to a lesser extent) the QC charms.<br /> But they'll still have the same Castes as Solars (but with different names and the slightly different caste powers... though I vaguely remember different caste powers being mentioned?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'd really like to see more of for Abyssals are mechanics that make use of your opponent's ones and failures. Whereas Solar heroes tend to rise to the occasion and get stronger as the opposition gets tougher, Abyssals have more talent for capitalizing on their opponent's mistakes. <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>While thematically, that's fine, I don't want to see it. I dislike all the charms that give you bonuses depending on your opponent's rolls, because they work out about the same, but slow things down slightly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:04:18-07:00","id":857198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856917#post856917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scroll of Heroes had, in its (yes, I know, terrible) merits section, a Past Life merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was originally in 1st Edition's Player's Guide as well which, while the various mechanical and setting expansions in it were not universally liked, they were also not generally regarded with the derision that everything but the Storytelling chapter in Scroll of Heroes is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856917#post856917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe the issue is that Exalted gets distracted by putting all those things onto Celestial reincarnation, which isn't really reincarnation at all.<br /> <br /> (Often, I just have my characters believe Celestial reincarnation is actually reincarnation, so that they can act like things like Oblivian are horrifying, believe going into Lethe is a good thing, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a big part of the problem as well. One of the big motifs for Solars is &quot;ancient heroes reborn in the world's hour of need&quot;, and the idea of &quot;lineages of heroism&quot; is important to the other types of Exalted, even if Dragonblooded are the only ones for whom it takes the form of passing it on to their children, so it makes sense that the past lives that the game wants you to focus on are the ones which are tied to your Exaltation. And I feel like it's been presented in a way that suggests that to characters subjective experiences, it should feel in all ways like one would expect remembering a past life to feel like. It's just that we, the players, overanalyze it and say that it's not &quot;real reincarnation&quot; because it's not the past of the hun soul that is being remembered. But that's also because of our assumptions of what identity is in modern western culture, which are not necessarily universal, and weren't always shared by the sources from which Exalted draws it's inspiration. I think doing as you suggest and treating it as real is probably going to produce the most satisfying results if you want to play up past lives in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T12:39:42-07:00","id":857248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857042#post857042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my understanding, John's idea is to start from the theme of excellence Abyssals share with Solars, and make their flashier stuff express the themes of the Deathlords just as Solars' flashy stuff expresses the themes of UCS. That doesn't sound like making them more like Solars if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly <i>hope</i> that's the intended application, but the wording still puts me on edge. And in my defense, how similar do the two splats actually need to be to draw a thematic parallel? I would posit that if Abyssals were known to be the product of Solar exaltation modification, shared a similar caste structure, and had access to the same tiers of power through necromancy, excellencies, mote pools and mastery keywords, that this would be more than sufficient for us to collectively agree that they are &quot;dark Solars.&quot; Basing even more of their charmset off of Solar powers seems overkill. It's not a bad idea in and of itself it just seems... unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T13:37:32-07:00","id":857265,"title":"","content":"Previous work John has done on Abyssals included a Larceny charm for replacing someones head with a pumpkin, whatever you might think of Malicious Parody Imposter and the other charms in that article it was pretty far from the recoloured death Solars they had been for most of 2e.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:34:07-07:00","id":857291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=856919#post856919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character is a solaroid exaltation\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. And not just because of the use of &quot;Solaroid.&quot; The Exaltation is not the character, the character is not the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the name of the game is not &quot;Exaltation.&quot; You play a hero imbued with the divine fire of the gods, not the divine fire itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T14:53:32-07:00","id":857301,"title":"","content":"I wonder how it is that one can read a preview and be put on edge by the things talking up the dichtomy with Solars while somehow entirely ignoring the ghostly chain whips that create iron maidens to crush people and turn them into zombie knights. Hell, going by what look like very strong parallels to the core Solar Presence Charms, some of the provisional Charms in the preview seem a lot like straightforward Mirrors and <i>still</i> work in a distinct way and create a distinct impression, such that I doubt anybody who looked at them the first time would have imagined they would have been so close to Solar versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:47:15-07:00","id":857324,"title":"","content":"Trying to think of something useful and constructive to contribute... Re: Charm sharing between Solars and Abyssals, it seems like one of those things you can't know what level is actually appropriate it is until you go through and look at it Charm by Charm?<br /> <br /> More broadly I think the essential thing with the Abyssals, like all Exalted, will be for the designers to imagine what the Abyssals will actually be doing in the stories - imagery, scenes, stories - and then work from that to give them the powers. For example, if you start with seeing an Abyssal full of undead resilience, as the Things That Will Not Die in your mind and then work back from that to Charms, if they converge with Solar Resistance, then OK, but they probably (or at least hopefully) won't. Where their stories and scenes naturally diverge from Solars (which they should), they'll naturally get Charms and magic that supports that. If their stories and scenes and images don't then, oh well, try and think of more stories. Take a Storytelling first approach - if you start with the idea that they should do this, this, and this and not this, as an abstract principle, without thinking of the images and stories first, you're constraining your view of things and maybe you'd end up with &quot;This is great, but what actually happens in their stories?&quot; sort of result. The 3e Solar Charms seem to work so well for all the fans (who like 3e's mechanical approach) because they're specifically inspired by being able to emulate specific stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T15:55:15-07:00","id":857325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857291#post857291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. And not just because of the use of &amp;quot;Solaroid.&amp;quot; The Exaltation is not the character, the character is not the Exaltation.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the name of the game is not &amp;quot;Exaltation.&amp;quot; You play a hero imbued with the divine fire of the gods, not the divine fire itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's, exactly my point? I dont know why you are picking a fight over nomenclature, but the fact is that the Deathlords want your exaltation, and they dont need you, personally. They can kill you and get back your actually valuable component at any time, and why wouldnt they when their pool of potential exalts is &quot;people who die?&quot; They have every oppurtunity to replace rebellious abyssals with loyalists of equivalent potential within a week or so in 2e canon.<br /> <br /> Also, could you please refrain from picking fights over minutia and taking the thread even further off topic? Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:13:25-07:00","id":857328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">their pool of potential exalts is &quot;people who die?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> About as much as the candidates for Solars are &quot;people who live&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T16:25:06-07:00","id":857331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857328#post857328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> About as much as the candidates for Solars are &quot;people who live&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar exaltations have specific and uncorruptible criteria for choosing exalts in Ex2, whereas the canonical rules for Abyysals is that the Deathlords personally choose who the exaltation goes to as long as it stays in a monstrance. Some have head canoned that they are still required to pick &quot;heroic&quot; mortals, but the only hard and fast rule in canon is that they have to exalt someone on the brink of death. So whereas a solar exaltation might take years to locate a suitable candidate, a Deathlord can pick some poor smuck tomorrow if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:08:09-07:00","id":857352,"title":"","content":"Disregarding subtext.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T17:43:57-07:00","id":857363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857352#post857352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disregarding subtext.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not. But if I were, it would be better than disregarding the actual text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:06:34-07:00","id":857374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857331#post857331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some have head canoned that they are still required to pick &quot;heroic&quot; mortals, but the only hard and fast rule in canon is that they have to exalt someone on the brink of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh no, if actual books say this then it's not headcanon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Scroll of Heroes, page 157</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><b>Abyssals </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">had the same capacity for heroism<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> and excellence as the Solars do, with one important<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> difference\u2014they were struck down by violence, disease<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> or simple misfortune before that excellence could fully<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> manifest itself. The characters must have been capable<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> of receiving a Solar Exaltation, but at the moment of<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> death, the Black Exaltation offers them a choice\u2014life<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> eternal in exchange for becoming a servant of death and<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> Oblivion. They must accept the Exaltation or die, but<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> they are always given a choice, and their damnation is<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> their own.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> Exalted 2e core, page 32</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><b>The Exaltation demands heroes. </b><span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Exaltation is a<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> fundamental alteration of destiny, turn a mortal into a<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> semi-divine weapon. To be capable of benefiting from the<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> Exaltation\u2019s power, the Exalt-to-be must already have an<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> important destiny. No Exalt is unwilling to wield his power.<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> The Exaltation is not a rational or moral force, though.<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> It simply seeks out beings who can and will wield divine<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> power. It could descend on the most pious of hermits or<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> the most immoral of rascals, so long as the chosen one is of<span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"> consequence to history and will put its might to use.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-01-2016, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:17:37-07:00","id":857378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857374#post857374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhh no, if actual books say this then it's not headcanon.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, my intrepration was that this was how the Abyssal exaltation WOULD work if not coopted by the deathlords, because otherwise I cant figure out how to reconcile this with the other rule that says Deathlords choose their Deathknights. Is this for sure a statment on how the exalatation process works with monstrances, or a separate rule? It would be nice if you were right about this honestly. At least then deathlords would be taking a gamble on their next chosen if they scrapped their rebels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:29:02-07:00","id":857382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857378#post857378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, my intrepration was that this was how the Abyssal exaltation WOULD work if not coopted by the deathlords, because otherwise I cant figure out how to reconcile this with the other rule that says Deathlords choose their Deathknights.</div> </div> </div> </div>They choose who to Exalt, but can only Exalt people of sufficient heroism just like they can only Exalt people who are on the brink of death. What's difficult about that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:54:36-07:00","id":857392,"title":"","content":"[Foffles] Hmm, this guy is on the brink of death and is of sufficient DETERMINATION to accept the Bargain.... BUUUUUUUT he's also incredibly angry at me for, you know, murdering his entire village with my zombie army, so maybe I SHOULDN'T give him power. Yeah... I think I CHOOSE to wait for someone comparably DETERMINED but a bit more pliable. Someone heroic but angry at someone else, so I can more easily point them in a direction of my choosing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T18:58:05-07:00","id":857393,"title":"","content":"Okay, these are good points. Ill post an excerpt of the rules from the monstrance spell when I get home, but this seems legit either way. How many people are heroic enough to be valid solar/abyssal candidates you think? Trying to get a sense for how big their pool of candidates would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:01:15-07:00","id":857395,"title":"","content":"Eh... 1 in 100? I don't know, I'm not sure there's a way to tell. It's probably not helpful to think of it like that.<br /> Essentially, to attract their attention, you're likely be doing something special anyway. I mean, if a town is being massacred by barbarians, they're not going to bother Exalting some scrub soldier to get vengeance, they're going to exalt the soldier who took 20 men down by himself, so he can go massacre the barbarians.<br /> The pool of candidates is far higher than the number of Exaltations they've got, so they're going to very picky anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857382#post857382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They choose who to Exalt, but can only Exalt people of sufficient heroism just like they can only Exalt people who are on the brink of death. What's difficult about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't really see an issue here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Previous work John has done on Abyssals included a Larceny charm for replacing someones head with a pumpkin, whatever you might think of Malicious Parody Imposter and the other charms in that article it was pretty far from the recoloured death Solars they had been for most of 2e. <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I think that charm's ridiculous... it wasn't like Solar charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I wonder how it is that one can read a preview and be put on edge by the things talking up the dichtomy with Solars while somehow entirely ignoring the ghostly chain whips that create iron maidens to crush people and turn them into zombie knights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this was the point I was trying to make earlier. The previews for Resistance and Presence, while clearly being Presence and Resistance charms, are not mirror charms. They're quite different from Solar charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-01-2016, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:19:39-07:00","id":857400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857325#post857325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's, exactly my point? I dont know why you are picking a fight over nomenclature, but the fact is that the Deathlords want your exaltation, and they dont need you, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Well, if that's your point\u2026 you're still wrong. As Lioness and others have said, their pool of people they select is fairly limited, and if they callously murder their Chosen for basically no reason, there's no guarantee that they'll be easily replaced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857325#post857325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, could you please refrain from picking fights over minutia and taking the thread even further off topic? Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put: I don't see it as off-topic. Abyssals will continue to be the dark reflections of Solars, and <i>as such</i>, it doesn't particularly strike me as fitting that paradigm for them to be perfectly servile, mind-raped automatons, only valuable for their magic black power pellet.<br /> <br /> I stand by my conviction that the kind of person who becomes a Solar (or in this case, an Abyssal) is made of sterner stuff than that, the kind of person who wouldn't let not being Exalted stop them from achieving something great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-01-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T19:36:29-07:00","id":857409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857400#post857400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put: I don't see it as off-topic. Abyssals will continue to be the dark reflections of Solars, and <i>as such</i>, it doesn't particularly strike me as fitting that paradigm for them to be perfectly servile, mind-raped automatons, only valuable for their magic black power pellet.<br /> <br /> I stand by my conviction that the kind of person who becomes a Solar (or in this case, an Abyssal) is made of sterner stuff than that, the kind of person who wouldn't let not being Exalted stop them from achieving something great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you... Under the impression that I like the state of affairs where Abyssals are slaves to Deathlord patrons? Because I dont. I dont understand the latter part of your comment. Are you saying that a mortal worthy of abyssal/solar exaltation wouldnt be a slave to the Deathlords? Because that's defiitely not true in Ex2. A mortal stands exactly zero chance against a Deathlord. And even if they could, an essential part of Abyssals being &quot;dark solars&quot; is that they CHOSE to become champions of death sworn to an evil lich. They chose to be slaves, instead of dying. If they hadnt chosen slavery, then they wouldnt be Abyssals. Are you advocating that we remove this element in Ex3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:01:06-07:00","id":857416,"title":"","content":"They aren't called death<i>slaves</i>. There's more freedom there than you're implying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:02:59-07:00","id":857419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857400#post857400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Well, if that's your point\u2026 you're still wrong. As Lioness and others have said, their pool of people they select is fairly limited, and if they callously murder their Chosen for basically no reason, there's no guarantee that they'll be easily replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they're the Dowager, who seems to have an endless supply of Shoats of the Mire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857416#post857416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't called death<i>slaves</i>. There's more freedom there than you're implying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the devs want to focus mostly on first ed, where Deathlords could kill an Abyssal anytime, no matter where they were. It was pitifully easy for them. One of the very few things Second did better for Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 04-01-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:09:34-07:00","id":857423,"title":"","content":"Focusing more on the 1st ed depiction doesn't mean copying literally everything. They've said several times that they don't want the Deathknights to just be minions of the Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:13:10-07:00","id":857426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857423#post857423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focusing more on the 1st ed depiction doesn't mean copying literally everything. They've said several times that they don't want the Deathknights to just be minions of the Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Far more so than in 2nd edition, at that. They've been quite explicit on a number of occasions that it's a master-apprentice relationship rather than a master-slave one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:33:45-07:00","id":857437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857416#post857416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't called death<i>slaves</i>. There's more freedom there than you're implying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't they be slaves? What leverage can a newly turned Abyssal use to get a better deal than that from their Deathlord? Or, what reason would a Deathlord ever have to demand anything less than perfect loyalty from their champion? Because with all the magical advantages a Deathlord has over their chosen, they certainly have the <i>power</i> to demand this fealty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:53:12-07:00","id":857451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857426#post857426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Far more so than in 2nd edition, at that. They've been quite explicit on a number of occasions that it's a master-apprentice relationship rather than a master-slave one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, considering the Deathlords, that seems a bit hard to believe. Or do masters regularly kill their apprentices on a whim (Dowager)? Do they fake their own death to manipulate the apprentices into doing exactly what they want (Eye and Seven Despairs)? And don't even get me STARTED on the Lover...<br /> <br /> It seems to me for that to work, they're going to have to burn the Deathlords (and possibly everything previously done with Abyssals) to the ground and start completely fresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":".  Adding reasons why 04-01-2016, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:58:01-07:00","id":857453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857451#post857451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me for that to work, they're going to have to burn the Deathlords (and possibly everything previously done with Abyssals) to the ground and start completely fresh.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is also one of the big 3e design goals. Something along the lines of &quot;having 9 clones of Adolf Skeletor as the undisputed and all-powerful gods of the Underworld is boring and dumb&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:03:14-07:00","id":857459,"title":"","content":"I welcome that change, but I feel like it'll be 3 years before I see if it actually happens. And part of me doubts that would happen, because there are people who'd flip out over it, and I wouldn't want any dev to have to take that sort of stuff on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T22:34:51-07:00","id":857514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857451#post857451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, considering the Deathlords, that seems a bit hard to believe. Or do masters regularly kill their apprentices on a whim (Dowager)? Do they fake their own death to manipulate the apprentices into doing exactly what they want (Eye and Seven Despairs)? And don't even get me STARTED on the Lover...<br /> <br /> It seems to me for that to work, they're going to have to burn the Deathlords (and possibly everything previously done with Abyssals) to the ground and start completely fresh.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't really have to start from scratch, they just have to make the Deathlords much weaker and more varied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T00:27:21-07:00","id":857553,"title":"","content":"Okay! For the reference of everybody who thinks that a Deathlord can/can't easily replace an Abyssal, here is some math:<br /> <br /> How many candidates does a Deathlord have to choose from in a given day? Well, our own planet has some 7 billion people, and on an average day 151,600 people die, according to Google. Factoring that out, we find that we lose about 0.002% of our population every day, worldwide. Let's assume that Creation has a similar rate of death to our real world, which for reference it would not. In the real world our biggest population centers live in close proximity to advanced medicine and clean food and water, considered luxuries by the vast majority of Creation. Also, we do not have actual monsters trying to kill us, just each other. And while terrorist attacks are scary, do they kill more or less people than fairy raids? Lots of factors, but 0.002% seems conservative to me.<br /> <br /> Now, how many people are in Creation? If anyone has a hard number I'd love to hear it. The best I could find was that the Blessed Isle has 100 million people following the end of the Great Contagion. Now that is the smallest of the five Directions, but assuming each Direction has at least that many people then that's roughly 500 million people in Creation. If 0.002% of them die a day, then that's 10,829 deaths each day.<br /> <br /> Now how many of those people are Solar material? One suggestion was one in every hundred, which would mean a Deathlord with an Abyssal exaltation has 108 souls to choose from on an average day that might make a half decent Abyssal. If it's more like one in every five hundred, then that would be 21 candidates. If it were one in every thousand, then just eleven. And if only one in every ten thousand mortals has the qualifications to be a Solar, then that's just one candidate a day, Creation-wide.<br /> <br /> On top of that, you need to match the exaltation's caste to the person. Now I have absolutely no idea what percentage of people are warriors, diplomats, priests, sages and thieves in Creation, but assuming an even split in potential you would take the above numbers and divide by five. So 21, 4, 2, or one every five days, depending on how uncommon you think Solar-worthy heroism should be. That's assuming they have their first pick of course, meaning no other Deathlord is currently in the market for a Deathknight. Which should be pretty rare I would think: they aren't exactly easy to kill.<br /> <br /> Now to me, these look like pretty expendable numbers. Like if I'm a Deathlord, I think I'm gonna live to see the end of time, and I'm willing to take my chances that with this many candidates popping up a day, that in any given week I'll find a really promising candidate just ripe for a bargain. And if not, there is nothing stopping me from creating a little chaos here or there, building up the death tolls and blaming the next Deathlord over if this produces a promising champion. As for my little problem Abyssal, well if I kill them directly through their monstrance then I loss the exaltation for a bit, which could be a problem, but nothing is stopping me from infecting them with the Plague and sending wave after wave of Bone Lions to wear them down and free up my prized black exaltation for a new, more compliant host.<br /> <br /> This is of course assuming that they rebelled in the first place, which is hard to imagine when you consider that at some point I brought them to my home in Stygia and gave them a stirring lecture with <i>at least</i> Performance eight and every solar/abyssal charm I qualify for, encouraging them to devote their life to my cause. Then, I sent them downstairs to meet <i>my</i> boss, who after looking into the depths of their soul and maybe even infecting them with Whispers, determined with infallible accuracy whether or not they believed in at least the core spirit of our cause. And if they had been found wanting, they would have died and their exaltation would have been returned to me at that time.<br /> <br /> <i>ALL OF THIS</i> needs to be addressed moving forward if we are going to have any hope of playing free Abyssals. Ignoring its presence will not make for a better setting or splat, it will just leave these problems for the next wave of simulationists to find and suffer through.<br /> <br /> TL,DR: There are plenty of heroic mortals dying in Creation, any one of which could replace a rebel Abyssal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-02-2016, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:15:58-07:00","id":857577,"title":"","content":"...Did this start out as an April Fools or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-02-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T01:39:50-07:00","id":857583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857577#post857577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Did this start out as an April Fools or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I love statistics. There is nothing funny about loving statistics. Statistics are <i>deadly</i> serious, and I have the statistics to back that up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T03:03:45-07:00","id":857601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857577#post857577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Did this start out as an April Fools or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>For my part, I am more pointing out something I felt was a bad bit of presentation of how Deathlords treat their Abyssals as expendable. There's a sense that a few might not be that way (I always got this feeling the Lion wasn't, if in part of his own sense of betrayal over having tried to do the &quot;right thing&quot; during the Contagion and getting punished for it. I can see him wanting to be different from that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:04:59-07:00","id":857612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857419#post857419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they're the Dowager, who seems to have an endless supply of Shoats of the Mire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a neat trick that is too. She raises an orphanage full of moppets in a Shadowland, <i>each with the potential excellence to exalt as a solar</i>, so she'll always have one <i>ready to accept exaltation</i> whenever she needs to replace the previous swamp piglet.<br /> <br /> Brilliant plan! What could <i>possibly</i> go wrong?<br /> <br /> (And why <i>hasn't</i> it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:30:36-07:00","id":857617,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Dowager's gone through that many Shoats of the Mire, yes there was the incident with Ragara Bhagwei but it's only been 5 years and no other indications that her rate of attrition is that high. There's more evidence that so many Sidereals died in the Usurpation that some of them had to have been killed repeatedly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:39:57-07:00","id":857618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857617#post857617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Dowager's gone through that many Shoats of the Mire, yes there was the incident with Ragara Bhagwei but it's only been 5 years and no other indications that her rate of attrition is that high. There's more evidence that so many Sidereals died in the Usurpation that some of them had to have been killed repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, it just seems odd they'd mention it if it wasn't a significant thing. Though it might just be she's sitting on some number of other Exalted. But even so, there are other Deathlords who seem less careful. I don't think Exalted should ever feel expendable (Tepet Lisara is one that bugs me for so many reasons, and I would love a change to her for the better).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:45:12-07:00","id":857620,"title":"","content":"It was a significant thing. Bhagwei may have potentially discovered the link between the Noss Fens and the Great Contagion which could being down heat on the Dowager that all the other Deathlords have avoided thus far.<br /> <br /> It's like the only plot hook that the Dowager has short of finding something in the Well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-02-2016, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T04:56:03-07:00","id":857626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857620#post857620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a significant thing. Bhagwei may have potentially discovered the link between the Noss Fens and the Great Contagion which could being down heat on the Dowager that all the other Deathlords have avoided thus far.<br /> <br /> It's like the only plot hook that the Dowager has short of finding something in the Well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant mentioning her cadre of potential Shoats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:25:47-07:00","id":857661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many people are heroic enough to be valid solar/abyssal candidates you think?</div> </div> </div> </div> Mu. (this forum is a graveyard for pithy answers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:35:42-07:00","id":857662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what reason would a Deathlord ever have to demand anything less than perfect loyalty from their champion?</div> </div> </div> </div> Politeness. With a little bit of fear. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">with all the magical advantages a Deathlord has over their chosen, they certainly have the power to demand this fealty.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did you <i>like</i> this in Second Edition? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And part of me doubts that would happen, because there are people who'd flip out over it, and I wouldn't want any dev to have to take that sort of stuff on.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well damn; I do believe we have here somebody who was won April Fool's Day in perpetuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T06:37:11-07:00","id":857665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857553#post857553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, you need to match the exaltation's caste to the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, while UCS basically does this instinctively, I don't think the Deathlords &quot;have&quot; to follow the same process (and we all know how easy it is to match Caste to concept/sheet even when it seems like it should be something else, because we want to be a certain Caste).<br /> <br /> At any rate, I think Deathlords can shoehorn any caste into any person they want. This may be somewhat inefficient, but practically it doesn't matter at all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857553#post857553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> with <i>at least</i> Performance eight and <b>every solar/abyssal charm I qualify for</b>, encouraging them to devote their life to my cause. Then, I sent them downstairs to meet <i>my</i> boss, who after looking into the depths of their soul and <b>maybe even infecting them with Whispers</b>,</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;assuming facts not in evidence for 3e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T07:56:49-07:00","id":857698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857662#post857662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And part of me doubts that would happen, because there are people who'd flip out over it, and I wouldn't want any dev to have to take that sort of stuff on.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do believe we have here somebody who was won April Fool's Day in perpetuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be honest, while I wouldn't put it quite like that, I did think the same thing as Isator: that's silly. Virtually no-one wants the Deathlords to stay as the masters of Abyssal slaves. No-one has complained about the way the devs want to reduce the way the Deathlords utterly dominate the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T08:02:49-07:00","id":857702,"title":"","content":"For me, it wasn't about &quot;nobody wants the Deathlords to be changed&quot;, it was &quot;I wouldn't want the developers to do a thing that people would flip out over them on&quot;. I mean, open your Third Edition corebook to a random spot and point at something; that is a thing that somebody has flipped out at the developers over. It would be nicer if we could do without it, but I think the developers are reasonably acclimitised to it being part of the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T08:07:51-07:00","id":857704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857698#post857698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be honest, while I wouldn't put it quite like that, I did think the same thing as Isator: that's silly. Virtually no-one wants the Deathlords to stay as the masters of Abyssal slaves. No-one has complained about the way the devs want to reduce the way the Deathlords utterly dominate the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Weeeell......not on <i>this </i>forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-02-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:08:29-07:00","id":857734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857665#post857665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;assuming facts not in evidence for 3e</div> </div> </div> </div>An important point: I'm <i>ONLY</i> talking about a <i>PROBLEM</i> I saw with second edition canon here. As I said in the conclusion, the many many advantages a Deathlord holds over their chosen champion is intensely problematic for allowing player agency as an Abyssal. Now this problem might <i>also</i> be addressed by a personality/mission statement change for the Deathlords, making them less objectively &quot;evil&quot; would free up some Abyssal narrative space, but this is how I see things standing in Ex2.<br /> <br /> Frankly, Deathlords were so powerful in Ex2 that even if they were a little softer and fluffier in Ex3 I'd still like to see them take a major nerf if only to allow other actors some time on stage in the Underworld. I loved the lore on the Lords of Stygia for example, but never used it in game because they were all so overwhelmed by the Deathlords that in practice they never felt relevant.<br /> <br /> Good point about castes, as well. I actually just ran a prelude game where our mortal heroes became Solars and on average I'd say each one of them could have been fit into at least three castes. So actually those prospective Abyssal rates would probably be higher, but I wanted to post a conservative number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:12:54-07:00","id":857737,"title":"","content":"I have no issues with the Abyssals being a dark corrupted Solar. The Deathlords all what 9 of them have a finite amount of Exaltations, this also plays into how they treat Abyssals. If destroying a portal is simple the problem that I see is what happens to the Exaltation I seem to recall if an Abyssal is redeemed the Monstrous cage of &quot;evil&quot; shatters freeing the Exaltation. So I would wager that while the Deathlords could destroy an Abyssal this way it would cost them an Exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:17:35-07:00","id":857778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857737#post857737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no issues with the Abyssals being a dark corrupted Solar. The Deathlords all what 9 of them have a finite amount of Exaltations, this also plays into how they treat Abyssals. If destroying a portal is simple the problem that I see is what happens to the Exaltation I seem to recall if an Abyssal is redeemed the Monstrous cage of &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; shatters freeing the Exaltation. So I would wager that while the Deathlords could destroy an Abyssal this way it would cost them an Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The official Ex2 canon rule is that a Deathknight who dies has their exaltation returned to its monstrance unless they are killed &quot;directly&quot; through their monstrance, in which case their cage breaks and the exaltation is free but still a corrupted abyssal exaltation. A free Abyssal exaltation can be summoned back into a fresh monstrance with a Void circle spell by any void circle necromancer, which is the main reason a Deathlord would not play this card: they are worried another Deathlord would pilfer their exaltation.<br /> <br /> As you say, Redemption also frees an Abyssal exaltation in canon, and there is no spell that can summom a solar exaltation back intobits monstrance. In other words, Redemption is the only canon way to actually escape a Deathlord's hold over your exaltation in the long term. Which gives them a very good reason to stop a Deathknight from achieving this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:41:44-07:00","id":857790,"title":"","content":"Well, there is also the other route, Immortal Malevolence Enslavement, which shatters your monstrous and puts you under the direct command of the Neverborn. This path is limiting in what characters can take it however as you have to wholly accept the Neverborns will and have no positive intimacies. I was personally always for a third path to freedom aside from redemption and full damnation and have written a good amount of homebrew to support it but aside from the suggestion of it as a play style in the storyteller section nothing supports it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T10:47:42-07:00","id":857793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>korekore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857790#post857790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is also the other route, Immortal Malevolence Enslavement, which shatters your monstrous and puts you under the direct command of the Neverborn. This path is limiting in what characters can take it however as you have to wholly accept the Neverborns will and have no positive intimacies. I was personally always for a third path to freedom aside from redemption and full damnation and have written a good amount of homebrew to support it but aside from the suggestion of it as a play style in the storyteller section nothing supports it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot that in Ex2 one of the canon paths to escaping your Deathlord was a deeper enslavement to an even worse entity... God what a choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:01:07-07:00","id":857803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857734#post857734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important point: I'm <i>ONLY</i> talking about a <i>PROBLEM</i> I saw with second edition canon here. As I said in the conclusion, the many many advantages a Deathlord holds over their chosen champion is intensely problematic for allowing player agency as an Abyssal. Now this problem might <i>also</i> be addressed by a personality/mission statement change for the Deathlords, making them less objectively &quot;evil&quot; would free up some Abyssal narrative space, but this is how I see things standing in Ex2.[</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't (and still don't) see where you were specifically talking about 2e, but ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:02:45-07:00","id":857804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857734#post857734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important point: I'm <i>ONLY</i> talking about a <i>PROBLEM</i> I saw with second edition canon here. As I said in the conclusion, the many many advantages a Deathlord holds over their chosen champion is intensely problematic for allowing player agency as an Abyssal. Now this problem might <i>also</i> be addressed by a personality/mission statement change for the Deathlords, making them less objectively &quot;evil&quot; would free up some Abyssal narrative space, but this is how I see things standing in Ex2.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's needs to be emphasized that 2e's Deathlord statblocks were a complete joke, and I am pretty sure nobody ever successfully used them for anything even in an elder game. You can't extrapolate anything about the Deathlords or the setting from them -- indeed, you can't really use them at all. They were carelessly done and, given that they're not of any value in a game either, should probably be ignored when reasoning about what Deathlords are capable of. It's not a coincidence that in 1e, Deathlords went almost the entire line without being tainted with stats, and the one place where they got stats is regarded as the low point of the entire edition.<br /> <br /> Having said that, though, if this is your sticking point, I wonder that you made a thread arguing that the problems with Abyssals came from a completely different source.<br /> <br /> (Haven't ignored your larger post but I needed to review some of the material myself before replying. Been a while.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 04-02-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:32:16-07:00","id":857824,"title":"","content":"I could have been much more clear that I was talking about a problematic thing from Ex2, in retrospect, and I'm sorry that important point got lost.<br /> <br /> (I'm glad someone is planning to address my Ex2 math, I worked really hard on that!)<br /> <br /> And I agree that the Ex2 Deathlords were, as written, toxic to the setting and pretty unuseable. I would not blame anyone for just ignoring them and their stats entirely, but we run a pretty simulationist game in our group, and attempts to include them as written in games has resulted in the frustrations I have been expressing above.<br /> <br /> I consider this a pretty solid reason to throw out their Ex2 stats and narrative and start over in Ex3.<br /> <br /> (EDIT) This thread did not start out as an argument for or against anything. Simply put: Abyssals have always been corrupted Solar exaltations, but the method of Solar exaltation has changed significantly in Ex3, and I'm trying to figure out what that means for Abyssals. They might still be corrupted Solars, but if Solar exaltation is something more like a personal choice that Sol makes now, how would anyone have corrupted that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-02-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:43:43-07:00","id":857861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857824#post857824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have been much more clear that I was talking about a problematic thing from Ex2, in retrospect, and I'm sorry that important point got lost.<br /> <br /> (I'm glad someone is planning to address my Ex2 math, I worked really hard on that!)<br /> <br /> And I agree that the Ex2 Deathlords were, as written, toxic to the setting and pretty unuseable. I would not blame anyone for just ignoring them and their stats entirely, but we run a pretty simulationist game in our group, and attempts to include them as written in games has resulted in the frustrations I have been expressing above.<br /> <br /> I consider this a pretty solid reason to throw out their Ex2 stats and narrative and start over in Ex3.<br /> <br /> (EDIT) This thread did not start out as an argument for or against anything. Simply put: Abyssals have always been corrupted Solar exaltations, but the method of Solar exaltation has changed significantly in Ex3, and I'm trying to figure out what that means for Abyssals. They might still be corrupted Solars, but if Solar exaltation is something more like a personal choice that Sol makes now, how would anyone have corrupted that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe the corruption is the Exalt themselves choosing themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T12:53:10-07:00","id":857869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857861#post857861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe the corruption is the Exalt themselves choosing themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Abyssal exaltation breaks the normal rules, which would be nothing new. I thought Ferryman made a good point about exigence black markets: if exaltations can be traded and stolen, that leaves room for the possibility of a Solar exaltation heist. Maybe the UCS gave his powers of exaltation away after the Usurpation, and it was from this lesser power that the black exaltations were taken? Or maybe they somehow stole the rights to Sol's power directly from the man himself. That'd be pretty hard, but I could believe it with a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T14:59:34-07:00","id":857947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might still be corrupted Solars, but if Solar exaltation is something more like a personal choice that Sol makes now, how would anyone have corrupted that</div> </div> </div> </div> People have probably overstated the degree to which the Essence of Exaltations are not things anymore. The mythology seems to present something that still exists enough that the Sidereal Exalted could seal it away, while being insubstantial enough to not be like a magical prosthetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:57:01-07:00","id":857972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857824#post857824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread did not start out as an argument for or against anything. Simply put: Abyssals have always been corrupted Solar exaltations, but the method of Solar exaltation has changed significantly in Ex3, and I'm trying to figure out what that means for Abyssals. They might still be corrupted Solars, but if Solar exaltation is something more like a personal choice that Sol makes now, how would anyone have corrupted that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of Morke's <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:damnation-101\" target=\"_blank\">past quotes</a> on Infernal Damnation Vs Abyssal Damnation might be enlightening to these questions, even if the backdrop regarding the Neverborn and the power of Oblivion likely no longer applies.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the idea that Abyssal Exaltation constitutes an inversion of Solar Exaltation, but the corruption of the latter was only possible because of its essential nature. That is to say, that Solar essence inherently had the potential to fall and become tainted in such a way as to create the Abyssal Exalted, which is the very thing that made their Redemption possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:25:39-07:00","id":858023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=857972#post857972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of Morke's <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:damnation-101\" target=\"_blank\">past quotes</a> on Infernal Damnation Vs Abyssal Damnation might be enlightening to these questions, even if the backdrop regarding the Neverborn and the power of Oblivion likely no longer applies.<br /> <br /> Specifically, the idea that Abyssal Exaltation constitutes an inversion of Solar Exaltation, but the corruption of the latter was only possible because of its essential nature. That is to say, that Solar essence inherently had the potential to fall and become tainted in such a way as to create the Abyssal Exalted, which is the very thing that made their Redemption possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a treasure trove of ideas, thank you for sharing this. To clarify, to what degree should these statements be taken as canon? A couple big points to draw attention to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Abyssals and Solars are a matter of transmission. <b>They are two halves of the same coin</b>, counterpart Exalted. In a word, the tragic fall to an Abyssal Exalted, or the heroic, arduous rise to a Solar Exalted, was<b> something built into these Exalts as a matter of fact</b>; of being able to tell the absolute pinnacle standby story of falling to the furthest depths of darkness or fighting your way back to light. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to mesh <i>really well</i> with what Haren suggested. Perhaps the Deathlords didn't directly corrupt the Solar exaltations, but found that they could corrupt the Sun's chosen <i>themselves</i> into accepting the dark half of Sol's power, something that had by natural law been there all along. Maybe something like a Monstrance torture chamber is still involved, or maybe we'll get tragic stories of Solars falling from grace in very personal ways. I believe its an Ex3 canon fact that there have been a handful of Solars in the world even as Sol has been turned away from it, maybe the Deathlords have been recruiting from that shallow pool over many centuries to gather their current forces?<br /> <br /> This reminds me of the story of the Ebon Dragon, and how none of his kin had taken notice of him until the Unconquered Sun took his true form for the first time. No one likes to talk about it, but maybe the USC creates as much darkness in the world as light?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John Morke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">...it would be doing Infernals a disservice if any path they take led them to becoming Solars. It sort of undercuts their mission and their thematic impact to even imply that they need to be Solars, in spite of whatever in-game reasoning there would be. It cuts the weight of the condition if, after some long transcendental quest, you could holy your way back into the Unconquered Sun's good graces and it resulted in you becoming a Solar Exalted, as if that were a superior state of being. Yes, for the purpose of being rid of your evil alien hellish connotations, it is, but the actual idea that you can fundamentally tear apart an Infernal Exalted and reach the Solar underneath goes against the entire metaphysical structure of what they are from top to bottom. It makes their Exaltation a bit less legitimate.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>And thank you, John, for clearly explaining everything I dislike about the Abyssal redemption arch. He's talking about Infernals here, obviously, but I've never understood why Abyssals got treated like the evil unwanted step children of second edition. Lest we forget, the way you <i>make</i> an Abyssal in Ex2 is by placing a normal Solar in a box and torturing them until their will breaks and they accepted the Black Exaltation in shame, which is not exactly an inspiring backstory for the splat. Having two sides to a coin is great, but clearly establishing one side as &quot;good&quot; and the other as &quot;bad&quot; does not leave us with equally appealing halves.<br /> <br /> In my ideal world, I hope that in Ex3 redemption continues to exist but that the choice to pursue it will not be so much presented as the only <i>proper</i> choice, and Abyssals will be appealing enough that Solar <i>characters </i>might want to make the switch. Perhaps the distinction would not be so much that Abyssals are &quot;failed&quot; Solars, but rather heroes of a variety that will cross any line to do what they think is right. So something like Captain America and the Punisher. People have strong preferences for one story over the other, but you could imagine a world where either one would want to be more like the other. Sorry, I'm ranting now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-02-2016, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:39:16-07:00","id":858029,"title":"","content":"I don't think you should take much of it as absolute, considering the context, but Abyssals still seem very intended to be dark reflections of the Solars (even as they're supposed to be their own thing as Death's Lawgivers and the exalted of the grave), and I find the link to be rich in pertinent thoughts on their relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T17:58:12-07:00","id":858046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=858029#post858029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you should take much of it as absolute, considering the context, but Abyssals still seem very intended to be dark reflections of the Solars (even as they're supposed to be their own thing as Death's Lawgivers and the exalted of the grave), and I find the link to be rich in pertinent thoughts on their relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an <i>extremely</i> useful read, thank you again for posting it. I am more or less sold on the idea that we should keep redemption and the Dark Solar angle around in Ex3, though again I <i>really</i> hope that with this new edition the writers will avoid the temptation to paint the Deathknights into an abysmally unlovable narrative corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:43:15-07:00","id":858067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">to what degree should these statements be taken as canon</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably not too much, since it's from a few years before Third Edition started, and is heavily referential to Infernals stuff that is long defunct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T19:14:55-07:00","id":858083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/855543-will-abyssals-still-be-dark-reflections-in-ex3?p=858023#post858023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, to what degree should these statements be taken as canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything outside of a published book or official blog (i.e. Ink Monkeys) is canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T23:04:49-07:00","id":858177,"title":"","content":"Regarding being able to 'lock up' Solar exaltations...<br /> <br /> I've come to see Exaltations as something more akin to a piece of reality than a thing; like a concept. Kind of like a title granted to you, like being president or the fastest man alive. And when you are bestowed that, it comes with boons. The Jade Prison did a hefty bit of reality shifting, and basically...folded that fragment of reality over and over again and bound it in metaphysical chains inside of a pandoras box equivalent.<br /> <br /> The lock was there, physically anchored on the Jade Prison, and when it was breached, that was the point where it all expanded back out into the world. So for a moment, that bit of reality was physically localized, which allowed the Deathlords to physically 'capture' those shards of existence that contained the specific ability for someone to be chosen as a Solar.<br /> <br /> That's my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}